# Cursor AI Agent Rules
# Personalized Travel Itinerary Planner — Skill Wallet Capstone

## Project Overview
This is a full-stack AI-powered travel itinerary planner.
- Frontend: React 18 + Vite + TypeScript + React Router
- Backend: Python + FastAPI + Pydantic
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- AI: Google Gemini API (google-generativeai)
- PDF: ReportLab
- Deployment: Frontend → Render, Backend → Vercel

## Project Structure
- `/frontend/` — React Vite TypeScript app
- `/backend/` — FastAPI Python app
- `/supabase/migrations/` — SQL schema files
- `/docs/` — Progress tracking and documentation

## Code Style Rules

### General
- Write clean, readable, production-quality code
- Add comments for non-obvious logic
- Never hardcode API keys, secrets, or passwords
- Always use environment variables for configuration
- Handle errors gracefully with meaningful messages
- Never expose sensitive data in logs or responses

### TypeScript / Frontend
- Use TypeScript with strict mode enabled
- Define interfaces/types in `/frontend/src/types/`
- Use functional components with hooks only (no class components)
- Put API calls in `/frontend/src/services/` — never in components
- Use React Router for navigation
- Name components in PascalCase, hooks as useXxx
- Use async/await, not .then() chains

### Python / Backend
- Use Python 3.11+ syntax
- All FastAPI endpoints must use Pydantic schemas for request/response
- Use async def for all endpoints that do I/O
- Keep routes thin — business logic goes in `/backend/app/services/`
- Database operations go in `/backend/app/database/`
- AI integration goes in `/backend/app/services/ai_service.py`
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes (200, 201, 400, 404, 422, 500)
- Log with Python's logging module — never log secrets

### Database
- All Supabase queries go through `/backend/app/database/`
- Never expose service-role key to frontend
- Use the anon key on the frontend only (when needed)
- Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection

### AI Integration
- AI provider logic is isolated in `ai_service.py`
- Always validate AI responses before storing or displaying
- Implement demo mode fallback when GEMINI_API_KEY is missing
- Never claim demo content is a live AI response
- Label demo content clearly

## Naming Conventions
- Files: snake_case for Python, kebab-case or PascalCase for React components
- Database tables: snake_case (trips, itinerary_days, activities)
- API endpoints: /api/v1/resource (plural nouns)
- Environment variables: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE

## Key Environment Variables
Backend:
- GEMINI_API_KEY — Google Gemini API key
- SUPABASE_URL — Supabase project URL
- SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — Supabase anonymous key
- SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — Server-side only
- DEMO_MODE — "true" to use fallback without AI key
- CORS_ORIGINS — Allowed frontend origins

Frontend:
- VITE_API_BASE_URL — Backend API base URL

## What NOT to do
- Never commit .env files
- Never put API keys in source code
- Never use hardcoded sample data as a substitute for real DB operations
- Never create fake buttons that do nothing
- Never claim external services work unless actually tested
- Never skip error handling
